est grossing films  in china have all been chinese with the  exception of avengers end game so you  know some things do cut through um but  what's interesting is that as china  rises um its own cultural exports are  becoming more um what it looks for so  and linda i know you wanted me to touch  on ways in which china is doing well as  well around the world um so you know  things like belt and road initiative we  talked about and of course peter is  right that a lot of these debt traps  leave countries in not very good  positions and we've heard about um sri  lankan ports being you know carved out  and all this sort of stuff but it's also  the case that um a lot of these  recipients of belt and road initiative  funding are not countries that the west  is interested in so when was the last  time that the uk did anything with  pakistan in terms of investment  so when was the last time that the uk  cared anything about africa you know we  earlier this year we had a debate about  the foreign aid budget cut  so it looks as if in a lot of these  places where perhaps because of the fall  of colonialism and imperialism the west  is withdrawing into itself with the  exception of tackling islamic extremism  perhaps whereas china is looking into  going to all of these places like  morocco like south africa like southeast  asia and giving them vaccines giving  them investments and that is one way in  which china is exporting its influence  but the question is about cultural  influence and this is the interesting  point i don't think it is exporting its  cultural influence except in cultures  that are already quite similar to itself  so in south korea japan southeast asia  there's a lot of consumption of chinese  soft power but outside of that it's not  this case that mandarin for example has  become  the language that everyone seeks to  speak i don't know if any of you have  even heard of chinese pop music and  certainly in a lot of parts of the world  that's not an export at al